. From the second equation, we obtain $x_3=0$. Substituting this into the first equation, we get $x_2=0$.\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535709 false] [17592186124251 1145 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =-4.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]-(-4)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5{x}_{2}+8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $2$nd and the $3$rd). Thus, $x_1$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain $x_3=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get $x_2=0.$ \n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069717/assets/4366abc9a1d46153708ef49ca06b25406739e06c5eaf3ee8c1a10c80081590f8.png)\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069717/assets/32cc18b0a63d50f6c20119cf7a437d7998123770320dcbfbe7e84f4833b2ff19.png)" 13194139535709 true] [17592186124252 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069717/assets/b065c3d310f87a61b96a72df966699f7f8497213a47e26d91b4ae93fc8b59c70.png)\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a basis of the eigenspace corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda=2?$" 13194139535709 true] [17592186124252 1100 "$\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -15 & 14 & -9 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a basis of the eigenspace corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda=2$?" 13194139535709 false] [17592186124252 1145 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation\n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2$. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA - λI &= \\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -15 & 14 & -9 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} - 2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -15 & 12 & -9 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{-10x_{1} + 8x_{2} - 6x_{3} = 0; - 15x_{1} + 12x_{2} - 9x_{3} = 0; - 5x_{1} + 4x_{2} - 3x_{3} = 0\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -15 & 12 & -9 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -15 & 12 & -9 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} + 3R_{1} \\\\\n&= R_{3}:=R_{3} + R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, $x_2$ and $x_3$ are free variables. From the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1=\\dfrac 4 5x_2-\\dfrac35x_3\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5}x_{2} - \\frac{3}{5}x_{3} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535709 false] [17592186124252 1145 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -15 & 14 & -9 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -15 & 12 & -9 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-10{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -15{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2}-9{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -15 & 12 & -9 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -15 & 12 & -9 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, $x_2$ and $x_3$ are free variables. From the first equation, we obtain $x_1=\\dfrac 4 5x_2-\\dfrac35x_3.$ So, the general solution is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refer